# OpenBot Environment Configuration Example
#
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTICE:
# - All API keys and secrets MUST remain server-side.
# - NEVER prefix secrets with NEXT_PUBLIC_ (which would bundle them into client JavaScript).

# Local model inference endpoint (Ollama-compatible /api/chat). Both are required.
# LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://localhost:11434
# LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=

# Model router (e.g. OmniRoute / 9Router / OpenRouter OpenAI-compatible endpoint).
# ROUTER_URL and ROUTER_MODEL are required; ROUTER_API_KEY is optional for local routers.
# ROUTER_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# ROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free
# ROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional external LLM provider (Anthropic API). Both are required.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Optional allow-list of model ids a bot may use in place of the global model
# (comma separated). When set, any other id gets 400 "model_not_allowed".
# When unset, any well-formed id is accepted.
# OPENBOT_ALLOWED_MODELS=vendor/model-a,vendor/model-b:free

# Access control for /api/*. Leave OPENBOT_ACCESS_TOKEN unset on localhost (open, as before).
# Unset, only loopback callers (127.0.0.1, ::1) are served; any other device gets a 403
# "access_token_required" until a token is set.
# When set, every /api call needs "Authorization: Bearer <token>"; in the browser save it with
# localStorage.setItem("openbot_access_token", "<token>").
# OPENBOT_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Requests per minute allowed per IP (default 60).
# OPENBOT_RATE_LIMIT=60
# Behind a reverse proxy you control (it always sets or appends X-Forwarded-For and is the
# only way in), set 1 so callers are counted per address (the last hop of that header).
# Unset, every caller shares one rate-limit bucket and one set of stream slots.
# OPENBOT_TRUST_PROXY=1
# Streamed replies open at once: per caller (default 4) and on the whole server (default 20).
# Over the cap, /api/chat/stream answers 429 {"error":"too_many_streams"}.
# OPENBOT_STREAMS_PER_CLIENT=4
# OPENBOT_STREAMS_GLOBAL=20
